.TH PROBENTIUM 1 "October 2026" "PROBENTIUM 0.2.0.dev3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
probentium \- offline evidence workbench with explicit uncertainty
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B probentium
.br
.B probentium
.RB [ \-\-format\ json ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B probentium console
.RB [ \-\-case
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-\-ascii ]
.RB [ \-\-no-banner ]
.br
.B probentium browse \-\-case
.I directory
.RB [ \-\-ascii ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PROBENTIUM acquires supported evidence, records byte provenance and maintains
revision-bound interpretations, conditional claims and reporting drafts.
It operates locally through commands and a keyboard terminal workbench.
With no arguments on an interactive terminal it opens the console.
Use console to select a case explicitly or disable the banner.
This version is a development preview.
.SH QUICK START
Create a synthetic exercise in a new directory:
.PP
.nf
probentium demo exercise
probentium verify \-\-case exercise/case
probentium browse \-\-case exercise/case \-\-ascii
.fi
.PP
Create a separate case and acquire a supported input:
.PP
.nf
probentium init investigation \-\-name "Local investigation"
probentium ingest \-\-case investigation evidence.jsonl \\
  \-\-format events-v2 \-\-label "Supplied evidence"
probentium timeline \-\-case investigation \-\-limit 25
.fi
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show command-specific help, examples, sensitivity and side effects.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the application version.
.TP
.B \-\-format json
Use the versioned JSON result envelope. This global option precedes the
command. The local ingest and inspect format option selects input syntax.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
For console or browse, render non-ASCII content using visible escapes.
.TP
.B \-\-no-banner
For console, suppress the introductory terminal logo.
.SH COMMAND GROUPS
.TP
.B init, demo, status, sources, ingest, inspect, timeline, event
Create cases, inspect or acquire supported input and inspect source records.
.TP
.B verify, resume, replay, recover, migrate, issues, support
Check integrity, continue interrupted intake and recover or report bounded state.
.TP
.B clock, claim, family, duplicates, identity, scenario, sensitivity, correlate, analysis, graph
Record interpretations and examine conditional findings, dependencies and limits.
.TP
.B control, incident, filing, diff, governance, legal, reporting
Manage supplied control observations and frozen reporting drafts.
No command submits a filing to an authority.
.TP
.B key, review, packet, parser-artifact, retention
Manage explicit trust, signed reviews, evidence transport, parser approvals
and authorized source-byte retention.
.TP
.B doctor, formats, schema, batch, browse, console
Inspect capabilities and contracts, run declared batch work or open the terminal.
.SH OUTPUT
Default command output uses JSON. The global JSON option returns an envelope
containing schema, status, case_revision, verification, data, limitations and
errors. Unknown revision or verification values remain null.
JSON uses ASCII escapes. Diagnostics use standard error.
Evidence output can contain sensitive case content or base64-encoded raw bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Operation completed; inspect its domain verdict and limitations.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid input, usage or an operation that could not be performed.
.TP
.B 3
Explicit partial availability or incomplete verification scope.
.TP
.B 4
Integrity, signature or binding verification failed.
.TP
.B 5
Revision, lock, hold or conflicting-state refusal.
.TP
.B 6
Resource budget exceeded or work aborted by a limit.
.TP
.B 7
Requested implementation or platform is unsupported.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted; inspect state before retrying a mutating operation.
.SH SECURITY AND LIMITATIONS
The local user, operating system, interpreter and installed dependencies are
trusted. Hashes prove consistency against a reference, not factual truth,
authorship or collection completeness. Signatures require independently
established key trust.
.PP
Case databases, indexes and source copies are plaintext. Optional age transport
encryption does not encrypt the local case. Retention does not promise secure
erasure. Draft legal profiles do not certify compliance or establish a verified
legal countdown. Linux is required for current strict resource enforcement.
.PP
A Debian installation does not become an approved wheel-distribution manifest.
Use only the explicitly supported parser provenance path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/probentium/schemas/
Installed machine-readable input contracts.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/probentium/
Usage, security limitations and packaging status.
